/* ================================================================================
   ██  DAILY DATA — EDIT THIS BLOCK ONLY, THEN RE-PUBLISH  ██
   ================================================================================
   Everything the dashboard shows for the LIVE (iBOS ERP) view is defined right
   here, at the top of the file. Nothing below this block needs to change for a
   routine data refresh.

   HOW TO REFRESH (daily/weekly):
   1. Re-extract the snapshot from the DWH (fin.tblAccountingJournalArc via
      MCP: mssql-test-server), or ask Claude to regenerate the CSV strings.
   2. Replace the five constants below with the fresh values.
   3. Update LIVE_ASOF to the extraction date, e.g. "2026-07-17 (embedded)".
   4. Save and re-publish the artifact (same link keeps working).

   WHAT EACH CONSTANT IS (all money in BDT crore; 1 Cr = 10,000,000 BDT):
   - LIVE_ASOF   : snapshot date shown in the header badge. Overwritten at
                   runtime only if a live MCP query succeeds.
   - COMPANIES   : [id, "Name", hasErpFeed(1|0)] for the company dropdown.
   - OPEN_CSV    : opening balances per company, one record per company:
                   "id,AR,AP,Cash,Inventory;..."
   - ARTOP_CSV   : top AR customers: "companyId|Customer Name|balance;..."
   - APTOP_CSV   : top AP suppliers: "companyId|Supplier Name|balance;..."
   - PL_CSV      : monthly P&L + balance movements, one record per
                   company-month:
                   "id,year,month,rev,oth,cogs,sm,logi,admin,mfg,depr,fin,tax,dAR,dAP,dCash,dInv;..."
   - DAILY_CSV   : same metrics at DAILY grain for the last ~92 days
                   (enables exact short date ranges: 2/3/7 days etc.):
                   "id,yyyymmdd,rev,oth,cogs,sm,logi,admin,mfg,depr,fin,tax,dAR,dAP,dCash,dInv;..."
                   Populated automatically by refresh_cfo_os.py. If empty, short
                   ranges fall back to a prorated monthly estimate (labelled).
   ================================================================================ */
